// B2 course (B1 → B2 roadmap), module 1 „Igapäevaelu ja B1 lähtepunkt” (b1b2-001…005), stage B1+ (001: B1).
// Lesson template v4 (docs/COURSE_DESIGN_COMMUNICATIVE.md §12). One storyline: the course's world one year later
// (docs/COURSE_CAST.md). Sofia passed B1 in May; Liis offers her the lead of Tuul Logistika's new Tartu warehouse project
// if she reaches B2 by March (partners, the city, negotiations in Estonian). The goal, said on the first sheet, sets up
// the whole B2 course; the module's goal: a diagnosis of the B1 base in situations, then a learning plan talked through
// with Liis and a written learning contract (004 Kasuta).
// No new grammar item: the module spirals the B1 core — the conditional for a polite request (001; again in 003's letter
// and 004's talk), linking words sest / kuna / kuigi / seetõttu / samas / enne kui / pärast seda kui (002; again in 003),
// time, frequency and duration with the verb second after an adverbial (003; again in 004), comparison — keskvõrre +
// kui, kõige, võrreldes + -ga, erinevalt + -st, mida … seda (004). B1 course words (koosolek, eesmärk, pakkumine,
// kokku leppima, tähtaeg…) come back.
// Harno B2 formats met in situations: a 4-option gap text (002), a lecture gap fill and a sentence-bank text (003), a
// debate with pro/contra cards ending in a decision and a semi-formal letter of ~140 words (003), a short work monologue
// (002, 003), multiple choice on meaning (004).
//   001 (diagnostic, B1) Liis's offer, Anna's diagnostic a year ago; the call to Keelekool Sõna (Maret), the diagnostic's
//       oral part; Sofia asks the head of personnel Eha Org for course support — a meeting and a formal request.
//   002 the team-day survey „how is your workday?”: Markus's voice message, Sofia's answer; warehouse shift leader Gert's
//       night shift, the newsletter; trainee Laura shadows Sofia — a text for the new-employee guide.
//   003 the team day in Pärnu with coach Hendrik Ilves: three rhythms, the time-use survey; Hendrik's talk on attention,
//       Jelena's meeting-free Wednesday; the debate (meeting-free day or a daily 15-min meeting) and the proposal to Liis.
//   004 when to study — Liis's and Markus's weeks; Helgi's letter, a radio programme with Maret; the learning-plan talk
//       with Liis and the learning contract (the module's final project).
// Lesson 5 (005) is the module's check in Harno form (unchanged). The v3 file is in archive/v3/b2/module01.js.
// Final shape (docs/COURSE_FINAL_SHAPE_B2.md §4.1, 2026-10-29): 001 LUGU R→W (main: W13 letter to Eha), 002 KUUL L→W
// (main: W05 guide text), 003 AVAS L→S (main: S17 argument cards; S16 talk recorded at home), 004 PROB R→S (main: S17
// learning-plan talk), 005 EKS. Every Kasuta has a home recording (S15/S16) and an in-lesson pair task; two fluency tasks a
// lesson (repeated talks with less time, 4-3-2 in 003). Task ids are tagged so that most catalogue types occur once.
